WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.199
Good morning, Hank. It's Friday, December
3rd. As you can possibly tell by the lamp

00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:07.549
shaped like a jellyfish, I'm not in my house.
Instead, Hank, I'm in Miami with its beautiful

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:11.660
beaches and its palm trees and its fancy art
fairs, none of which I get to enjoy! Because

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.840
even though I mentioned earlier that it is
December 3rd, I still haven't finished NAFADOYBIMSCOM,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.460
NAtional Finish A Draft Of Your Book I Mean
Seriously Come On Month! It's like it's still

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.460
November! Ahhhhh! I'm a giant squid of anger!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.369
Well, Hank I've got to put aside the giant
squid of anger in my heart because today we

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:32.200
have to talk about giant squids of love. But
even more importantly, I want to discuss with

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.120
you why I am so fascinated by the sex lives
of species different from us.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:42.170
Okay, Hank, so here is the giant squid: Majestic,
very secretive. We don't know what they eat.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.221
We don't know how deep they're able to dive.
We don't know what they do for fun. And we

00:00:45.221 --> 00:00:50.160
don't really know for sure how they mate.
But we've got some ideas, and they involve

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.850
penile fire-hoses. Alright, Hank, so most
squid have eight arms; two longer tentacles

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:01.990
that they use for feeding; and one hectocotylus,
which is kind of like a penis except it falls

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.890
off every time they have sex. Like, they put
it into the girl squid, and then the girl

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:10.600
squid kind of breaks it off. Giant squids
don't have a hectocotylus, instead they have

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.330
a three-foot-long penis, and like a lot of
invertebrates they produce spermatophores,

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:18.710
which are like these sacks that contain sperm.
But, unfortunately, female giant squid anatomy

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.380
doesn't really give you a convenient place
to put that spermatophore, and that's where

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.790
the fire-hose comes in.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.160
Hank, in the last 48 hours I've read so much
about giant squid sex that I'm surprised the

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.170
hotel still lets me have internet. And so,
I can tell you that without fail researchers

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:37.750
who are hypothesizing about giant squid sex
always refer to the male squid penis as a

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.070
fire-hose. Because what they think happens
is the male squid's penis approaches a female

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:49.490
squid's arm and then, like a fire-hose, shoots
a spermatophore into the arm. At which point,

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.610
the female, as you can imagine, is like "Oh!
What did you just do to me!" Which is actually

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.900
bad for the males because the females are
much larger, and that, biologists think, is

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.300
why the male squid penis is so long: so they
don't have to get too close to the females

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.700
in order to inseminate them.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.630
Now, Hank, I'm not an expert in the field,
but it seems to me that fire-hosing your spermatophore

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:12.490
into a lady arm is not a pleasant or even
very efficient method of reproduction. And

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:18.130
it makes me wonder: Why? Why don't they just
find a better way to do it? But from an evolutionary

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:21.640
perspective, is it ultimately more helpful
to have an efficient mating system, or is

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:27.110
it more helpful to have, say, an eye that's
a foot freakin' wide, which is what giant

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.630
squids have. In fact, we see examples over
and over in our world - we've been talking

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.730
about them all week - of incredibly inefficient
mating. Hank, its almost as if sex is not

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.190
actually the most important thing that animals,
including humans, do. And Hank, I believe

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:43.520
that is one thing giant squids are trying
to tell us. I've got to go back to my story,

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.050
but Hank I will see you on Monday.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:50.800
Ah! Nerdfighters, I almost forgot, but because
you proved that space pasta is far less efficient

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.099
than Earth beef, you now get to challenge
us to do something difficult and/or horrible.

00:02:56.099 --> 00:02:59.830
I should add, however, that a nerfighter named
Stanage did some research suggesting that

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.830
space pasta might actually be more efficient
than Earth beef if we use the space shuttle

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:07.940
to pick it up instead of Apollo 11, provided
that there was already space pasta on the

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:11.810
moon. But sadly, at least as far as we know,
there isn't space pasta on the moon. At any

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:15.660
rate, you figured it out so you get to challenge
us. Leave you suggestions for challenges in

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:20.000
the comments and upvote you favorites and
as always: DFTBA.

